UID:260612d-B8g8bg0UeC6kVrxle2pQ
DESCRIPTION:Weekly Sessions | Grades K - 8 | Various Locations Ignite curi
 osity\, creativity\, and adventure this summer! Summer WonderCamp invites 
 children entering grades K-8 to dive into hands-on STEAM explorations\, ou
 tdoor adventures\, and imaginative play. Each week\, campers shape their o
 wn learning through themed experiences - tinkering and inventing\, cultiva
 ting gardens\, tracking birds\, experimenting with chemistry\, designing h
 abitats\, and more. With dedicated mentors\, small-group support\, and rea
 l-world tools\, campers build confidence\, collaboration\, and wonder in a
  safe and supportive environment. Summer WonderCamp is where discovery\, s
 cience and fun meet! Member Registration opens Tuesday\, February 17\, 202
 6 Non-member Registration opens Wednesday\, February 18\, 2026 Scholarship
 s Available  Learn More
LOCATION:Wonderlab
URL:https://wonderlab.org/event/summer-wondercamp/2026-06-15/
X-SOURCE:Limestone Post
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Traveling Town Hall with Mayor Thomson
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260615T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260615T193000
UID:260521ClhQdDy-0Uyge5U44mSjzg
DESCRIPTION:Join Mayor Kerry Thomson for the District 6 Traveling Town Hal
 l on Monday\, June 15th\, 2026\, from 5:30 to 7:30 p.m. at Monroe County H
 istory Center\, 202 E 6th St\, Bloomington\, IN 47408.This event offers re
 sidents the chance to connect directly with City leaders\, ask questions\,
  and learn more about key projects and city services.The evening will begi
 n with brief updates from the Mayor\, followed by a Q&A session based on s
 ubmitted questions. If time allows\, the event will conclude with live que
 stions from attendees.Traveling Town Halls are held in a different distric
 t every other month as part of the City’s commitment to transparent\, ac
 cessible government. Anyone interested in how city services are delivered 
 is encouraged to attend.The meeting will be broadcast live on Community Ac
 cess Television Services (CATS) and available for on-demand viewing at ca
 tstv.net.
LOCATION:Monroe County History Center
URL:https://limestonepost.org/calendar/#/details/traveling-town-hall-with-
 mayor-thomson/18965746/2026-06-15T17
X-SOURCE:Limestone Post
END:VEVENT
