BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Event Details From: July 25\, 2026 To: July 26\, 2025 Starting at:
  02:00 PM Finishing at: 10:00 PM
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260725T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260725T140000
UID:2512184DSri1FDrEWNun965Oe3Kw
DESCRIPTION:Join us for our Fire@Nite public event on July 26th from 2-10 
 pm! Experience the unique art form of cast iron as the Trails Artists crea
 te stunning performances throughout the day. Explore the extensive collect
 ion of sculptures while hiking the Trails. Your fun-filled schedule for th
 e day: From 2-7 pm Witness performances throughout the museum involving ca
 st iron\, and be sure to hike the Trails to explore the variety of sculptu
 res in the museum's collection. Also\, meet the Trails Crew that have trav
 eled worldwide to become an artist intern at the museum during the month o
 f July. Interested in creating your very own cast iron art? Join us at our
  carving zone\, where the Sculpture Trails crew will be ready to help you 
 make your own relief sculpture and cast iron bowl during the event. Enjoy 
 the experience of watching as your art gets poured with molten metal durin
 g the main performance at 8 pm. Scratch Blocks and Doodle Bowls will be av
 ailable to purchase until 7 pm or until supplies last. Why Wait?! Purchase
  your scratch blocks and doodle bowls in advance!! Scratch blocks are a $2
 5 donation\, and Doodle Bowls are a $50 donation to the museum. You can st
 op by the Trail's foundry anytime before the event and purchase one from t
 he Artist in Residence. From 8-10 pm Starting at 8 pm the main foundry wil
 l pour over 3\,000 pounds of cast iron using two large-scale cast iron fur
 naces. Witness large metal sculptures being poured and performance art don
 e by artists from all over the world. Come on out and share this unique ex
 perience with us as our July Workshop comes to a fiery close! For more inf
 ormation about Fire@Nite Please contact Gerry Masse by phone call or text 
 at \\(502-554-1788\\) or email \\( \\).
LOCATION:Sculpture Trails
URL:https://sculpturetrails.com/mevents/annual-firenite-iron-pour-2026/
X-SOURCE:Limestone Post
END:VEVENT
